; arena.eval — the controlled space, exercised.
;
; The showcase level fought every attempt to measure anything in it (a monster
; already adjacent, an unwalkable target cell, one that would not engage). This
; builds its own room instead, and everything in it was put there on purpose.
;
; The map is 28x24, so the arena centres on 14,12. Those coordinates are
; hardcoded below because a script cannot read a command's answer — the `arena`
; line PRINTS its bounds so a log reader can confirm they were what was assumed.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 11

; MAPINFO AFTER EVERY CARVE. The `arena` line reports its BOUNDS, and for a
; `room` those bounds are a bounding box: `arena room 7 6` prints
; `floor 11,9..17,21` — 91 cells — of which 55 are carved and 36 are rock
; (docs/eval-audit.md F14). The walkable count is the only readout that can tell
; the difference, and it is the only one that can see an arena that never came
; back at all.

; --- 1. an open room, one monster, one fight ------------------------------
arena open 9 9
mapinfo
spawn skeleton 14 8 south
tp 14 12
echo --- open: before ---
party
monsters
step 30
echo --- open: after ---
party
monsters

; --- 2. HIS BLAST CASE: one in the middle, eight around it ----------------
; A fresh room wipes the previous fight entirely, so this starts clean.
arena open 9 9
mapinfo
spawn skel_swarm 13 11 south
spawn skel_swarm 14 11 south
spawn skel_swarm 15 11 south
spawn skel_swarm 13 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 14 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 15 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 13 13 south
spawn skel_swarm 14 13 south
spawn skel_swarm 15 13 south
echo --- 3x3 surround: nine placed ---
monsters

; --- 3. the geometries a blast reflects in --------------------------------
arena corridor 11
mapinfo
echo --- corridor ---
monsters
arena deadend 7
mapinfo
echo --- dead end (centre IS the closed end) ---
arena tjunction 9 5
mapinfo
echo --- t-junction (centre IS the junction) ---
state
